@tradition seed-packet-day
// Round 2 (seasonal): Ravi Hart draws next season's seed packets and everyone folds and fills one with their own drawing. Once a season, week 4's Saturday (Day 27, 118...).
// Rules: FX24 (0.93.2, behind TRAD_0932_ON in section 13). Words: CS1 (plans/trad-0932-words.txt, claude/crew-stories-pitch 7b1e7300).
// Host check (FX24): the card's 11:00 is inside Ravi's garden shift (06:00-14:00, Saturdays), and garden hour has the garden 14:00-15:00, so 16:30-17:15.
k: 1313
title: Seed packet day
when: quarter week 4 saturday
at: 16:30-17:15
min: 20
where: 3 pool garden
who: hart-ravi always, cruz-tove 70%, gardener 45%, garden-lover 35%, everyone 8%
anim: hart-ravi talk, everyone fold
host: hart-ravi
from: hart-ravi
invite: host=hart-ravi odds=25% line="Seed packet day in the garden. Draw your packet. Cruz sows what's in it next season."

== mail
- Seed packet day tomorrow, {time}, in the garden. Fold a packet, fill it, draw on the front. Next season's sowing comes out of them. I'll bring the pencils.

== ask
- Seed packet day in the garden. Ravi's drawing the beans. They look like ducks.   #funny
- Making seed packets later. Your drawing goes in the garden for a season.
- Coming to seed packet day? It's once a season. Don't miss it.

== here
- Fold, fill, seal. Then draw.
- What's yours? Carrots? Draw a carrot.
- That's a good packet. Cruz will like that one.
- Don't drop the seeds. They're very small and very fast.   #funny

== thanks
- You fold a seed packet, fill it from the jar, and draw on the front. Next season, Cruz sows it.   #warm

== chatter
- My seed packet has a drawing of a tomato. It's mostly a circle.   #funny
- Cruz kept all the seed packets in a tin. Every single one.   #warm
- Seed packet day means a new season's coming. Feels like it, anyway.
